# Corpus unit fre/C01 — justified (generalization; controlled_comparison)
#
# Source: m0/annotations/fre.yaml C01 (generalization, double-annotated; corpus pin 62e9b54).
# Headline: using only K=32 (state, reward) pairs per task, FRE-all reaches an overall normalized
# score of 57 +- 9 vs SF 33 +- 12, GC-IQL 24 +- 12, GC-BC 18 +- 5 (FB/SF use K=5120), competitive
# or better across AntMaze/ExORL/Kitchen over 5 seeds.
#
# Lowering notes (conventions: corpus-units/LOWERING.md):
#   * Family map: controlled_comparison. Nearest-competitor convention: B = SF, the strongest
#     non-privileged baseline on the aggregate 'all' row (FRE 57 vs SF 33); GC-IQL, GC-BC, FB, and
#     the privileged OPAL are dominated a fortiori and stay in `nl` and refs. Q = zero_shot_return,
#     D = eval_suite (AntMaze/ExORL/Kitchen).
#   * KEY judgment (uniform-standard rule, recorded per LOWERING.md). The annotation's mandatory
#     CQ3 asks for a statistical significance TEST across the 5 seeds and is rated unmet-gap. Its
#     nearest policy-mandatory CQ is variance_reported, whose bar is only that variance be reported
#     — and FRE reports mean +- std over 5 seeds, so variance_reported(e01) is FACTUALLY MET and is
#     discharged. corpus-v1 has no significance-test CQ; the annotator's stronger demand is a policy
#     vocabulary gap, noted here, not a hole in an accepted unit. This is the mirror image of
#     adaptive-pruning/C03 (no seeds AT ALL -> variance genuinely unmet -> gap): the policy call
#     wins in both directions.
#   * CQ1 (same datasets/episodes/normalization) discharges baseline_parity; CQ2 (K=32 vs K=5120
#     budget asymmetry disclosed and, if anything, disadvantaging FRE) discharges measurement_
#     validity. The optional scope_match has no annotated met basis (the only optional-scope CQ,
#     reproducibility/hardware, is unmet), so it is declared an `open` hole — corpus-v1's question-
#     coverage rule (Check.Support R5) requires every rule question to be discharged or open, and an
#     open OPTIONAL question adds no obligation (openMandatory filters to mandatory), so a1 stays
#     complete. The optional OPAL-privilege caveat (met) is subsumed in nl. All three mandatory CQs
#     met -> complete support -> justified.
#
# Expected verdict is at the bottom of this file (golden oracle).

artifact fre at sha256:c1bb86743873
policy corpus-v1
use backends [nd@1]

# --- The headline claim ------------------------------------------------------------------------

claim c01
  nl      = "Using only K=32 (state, reward) pairs per task, FRE-all reaches an overall normalized score of 57 +- 9 vs SF 33 +- 12, GC-IQL 24 +- 12, GC-BC 18 +- 5 (FB/SF use K=5120), competitive-or-better across AntMaze/ExORL/Kitchen over 5 seeds"
  formal  = better(fre_all, sf, zero_shot_return, eval_suite)
  binding = { author = m0-annotator, audit-status = reviewed }

# --- Evidence leaves ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

leaf e1 : reports(e01, compares(fre_all, sf, zero_shot_return, eval_suite, favorable))
  kind       = observed
  provenance = ai-executed
  refs       = [evidence/tables/table1_main_results.md, Table-1-row-all]

leaf e2 : matched_setup(fre_all, sf, e01)
  kind       = attested
  provenance = ai-executed
  refs       = [logic/experiments.md#E01-Procedure-steps-1-7, Table-1-Conditions]

leaf e3 : valid_measurement(zero_shot_return, e01)
  kind       = attested
  provenance = ai-executed
  refs       = [logic/experiments.md#E01-Procedure-steps-4-7, Table-1-caption]

leaf e4 : variance_reported(e01)
  kind       = observed
  provenance = ai-executed
  refs       = [evidence/tables/table1_main_results.md, logic/experiments.md#E01-Metrics]

# --- The support argument ----------------------------------------------------------------------

arg a1 : supports(c01) by controlled_comparison(fre_all, sf, zero_shot_return, eval_suite, e01)
  discharge baseline_parity      with e2
  discharge measurement_validity with e3
  discharge variance_reported    with e4
  open      scope_match          as scope_match

status c01

# ==============================================================================================
# EXPECTED VERDICT (golden oracle)
# ==============================================================================================
# Compiled AF: a1 alone, unattacked -> in (grounded).
# Claim status:
#   c01 -> justified (its complete support a1 is `in`; spec §8 aggregation)
